WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.929
Inside you, right now, five
organs are hard at work.

2
00:00:08.149 --> 00:00:11.586
Each one has a job. Your
body needs every one of them.

3
00:00:12.086 --> 00:00:15.662
An organ is a part inside
your body with a job to do.

4
00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:19.411
You cannot see them with your
eyes. Here is where they sit.

5
00:00:19.631 --> 00:00:25.158
Today you will meet five. The brain,
in your head. The lungs, in your chest.

6
00:00:25.378 --> 00:00:29.371
The heart between the lungs, the
stomach, and the intestine below.

7
00:00:29.871 --> 00:00:33.029
The brain sits in your
head, inside your skull.

8
00:00:33.249 --> 00:00:36.129
It thinks. It remembers. It feels.

9
00:00:36.349 --> 00:00:39.181
And it tells every other
part of you what to do.

10
00:00:39.401 --> 00:00:43.813
The lungs are in your chest. They
take air in when you breathe in.

11
00:00:44.033 --> 00:00:47.284
They push it out again when
you breathe out, all day long.

12
00:00:47.784 --> 00:00:52.335
The heart sits between your two
lungs, in the middle of your chest.

13
00:00:52.555 --> 00:00:57.013
Many children put it on the far
left. It is really in the middle.

14
00:00:57.233 --> 00:01:00.763
The heart is a pump. About
once a second, it squeezes.

15
00:01:00.983 --> 00:01:04.048
Each squeeze pushes blood
round your whole body.

16
00:01:04.268 --> 00:01:08.587
Blood carries food, and the goodness
from the air, to every part of you.

17
00:01:08.807 --> 00:01:11.686
Put a hand on your chest
and feel it beating.

18
00:01:12.186 --> 00:01:15.065
When you swallow, food
goes down to your stomach.

19
00:01:15.285 --> 00:01:19.419
The stomach is a stretchy bag.
It churns the food into mush.

20
00:01:19.639 --> 00:01:24.236
The stomach is not your whole tummy.
It is one bag, up under your ribs.

21
00:01:24.456 --> 00:01:28.682
Then the mush moves into the
intestine, a long coiled tube.

22
00:01:28.902 --> 00:01:32.385
The goodness passes through
its walls and into your blood.

23
00:01:32.885 --> 00:01:36.879
We cannot look inside ourselves,
so scientists use models.

24
00:01:37.099 --> 00:01:41.371
A diagram is one kind of model.
It is a drawing with labels.

25
00:01:41.591 --> 00:01:45.028
Today you will put five labels
on a picture of the body.

26
00:01:45.248 --> 00:01:49.242
Brain, lungs, heart, stomach,
intestine. That is a diagram.

27
00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:52.946
Another kind of model is
one you can make and touch.

28
00:01:53.166 --> 00:01:57.299
A grown-up cuts the bottom off a
bottle. The bottle is your chest.

29
00:01:57.519 --> 00:02:02.117
A balloon hangs inside it, from
the neck. That balloon is a lung.

30
00:02:02.337 --> 00:02:07.074
A second balloon stretches across the
bottom. That is the breathing muscle.

31
00:02:07.294 --> 00:02:12.913
Pull the bottom balloon down, and the
lung fills with air. Breathing in.

32
00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:19.681
Let go, and the lung empties.
Breathing out. Your model breathes.

33
00:02:20.181 --> 00:02:23.664
Brain thinks. Lungs
breathe. Heart pumps blood.

34
00:02:23.884 --> 00:02:27.878
The stomach breaks food down.
The intestine takes the goodness.

35
00:02:28.098 --> 00:02:31.906
A diagram and a bottle of balloons
are both models of your body.

36
00:02:32.126 --> 00:02:36.166
Five organs, five jobs, all
working inside you right now.
